  checkpoint: MiniModel.org ef924db7b721ed3fea371fb3f29416261d8f31b8
  change: Removed copied-site snapshots, their Win32 directory identity/cleanup and BlobReader test hook. Publication uses bounded canonical Git/current bytes held and authenticated in memory; upload and rollback consume that bound input.
  evidence: MiniModel.org/artifacts/reports/publication-input-review-20260912.json
  lessons: wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/ecosystem-experiment-lessons-2026-09-12.md C23
  verification: All 53 Node and 24 nested Pester checks pass, zero skipped/cancelled. Current catalog Git/input admission and historical 422-byte versus current 593-byte rejection were exercised. Actual file publisher tests retain predecessor backups and refuse substituted bytes. Whole-module command coverage 238/545; no branch or actual FTPS claim.
  remaining: Fresh release identity and stale bound deployment manifest, intentionally unbound transport, real model qualification and seed hosting. The following checkpoint addresses the Node launcher and metadata generator. Owned test output was removed; no publication, model deletion or measured storage recovery.

