  environment_lock: contracts/vnext/qwen3-numerical-oracle-environment-lock.v2.json
  differential_profile: contracts/vnext/qwen3-numerical-differential-profile.v2.json
  change: Rebuilt one exact canonical runtime from 31 verified wheel identities. Current source/reconstructed producers and verifier bind the new environment/profile; source validation uses the corrected licensed source lock. The new profile explicitly requires fresh execution orchestration and does not adopt closed v2 authority.
  verification: Actual source-owner environment admission passes; 28 distributions and 17677 files validate. All 25 focused Node, eight Python and five cleanup Pester checks pass with zero skips. Ruff passes. Cleanup command coverage is 86/132, below target because destructive removal and receipt writing were not executed.
  pending_cleanup: Automatic review rejected the failed bootstrap removal and the two exact virtualenv capability-probe link removals. The unchanged source-authority scan is incomplete on those links. The installer root contains 431 regular files, 93 directories, two links and 296933889 logical bytes; no parent deletion or alternate API was used to retry a rejection.
  owner_cleanup: tinyrustlm/tools/remove-reviewed-numerical-installer-output.ps1; actual WhatIf preflight verifies the complete exact inventory. Run only by the owner after reviewing the pending cleanup; the retained canonical runtime is excluded.
  remaining: Remove the blocked temporary output and rerun the unchanged source gate; finish fresh numerical owner/registration bindings and real model qualification. No real checkpoint load, numerical parity, working default, live seed, deployment or measured storage recovery is claimed.

numerical_execution_boundaries:
  evidence: artifacts/ecosystem-cleanup-20260912/numerical-execution-boundary-review.json
  lessons: wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/ecosystem-experiment-lessons-2026-09-12.md C29
  change: Canonical request/output/model locations, minimal child and termination environments, isolated Python startup, explicit empty NODE_V8_COVERAGE and unchanged source-authority preflight. Both affected fixture families use owned canonical artifacts and inline probes.
  verification: All 56 affected checks pass with zero skips. Actual Node and pinned Python probes pass; framework tests are synthetic. V8 ranges reached 53/54 selected source lines in the three new boundary functions; no whole-owner or branch percentage. Owned test/coverage output removed.
  experiment: The first instrumented suite had three launch failures because Node automatically copied ambient coverage into the frozen child environment. An explicit empty own property fixes both mutation and output inheritance; the failure and exact installed Node implementation are recorded.
  remaining: Source scan is still incomplete on the two policy-blocked C28 links. Closed v2 metadata coupling remains; prepare fresh owner, registration and dependency bindings before a real operation. No real checkpoint, qualification, default, seed, deployment or measured storage recovery.

